Screen
/ PlangOS's shell: part of the system (plang's os folder, read-only, comes with the image), run in
/ the person's app, /home/plang — their files, their .db. Host plang starts it (wsl … --cd
/ /home/plang … /opt/plang/plang system/plangos/Screen).
/ PlangOS's side of the screen. The
/ screen is PlangOS's display: programs draw onto it, and its frames go to this app's output —
/ the pipe to host plang. Input from the host comes down on stdin, one line per event, and goes
/ to the screen. Ends when the host closes the pipe.
/ The first page is the desktop; every app opens in a window of its own.
- screen.open(ToOutput=true, OnWindow=goal.call(Name="Window")); variable.set(Name=%screen%, Value=%!data%)
- browser.start(Url="file:///opt/plang/os/system/plangos/desktop.html", Screen=%screen%, OnMessage=goal.call(Name="Desktop")); variable.set(Name=%browser%, Value=%!data%)
/ A question for the user (a permission, `ask user "…"`) is a dialog on the screen: asked on the
/ console, it would go into the screen's pipe and wait on the host's input.
- channel.set(Name="input", Goal=goal.call(Name="Question"))
/ Every error — in the shell's goals, a click's or a window's callback, the system's own — shows on the desktop's
/ taskbar: nothing fails where no one sees it.
- channel.set(Name="error", Goal=goal.call(Name="ShowError"))
/ the desktop's files, once %browser% is known (the page itself can't ask: it loads while browser.start runs)
- goal.call(Name="Files")
/ new files for this shell, if the host has any — in parallel, so the shell starts anyway
- goal.call(Name="Update", Parallel=true)
/ what runs (the host's plang and the image), on the taskbar — in parallel too
- goal.call(Name="Version", Parallel=true)
/ ☰ on a window is its agent: Claude, who works on the window's app with the person, through plang.
/ (on click on #window.bot, call ShowClaude — formal until the builder learns # elements)
- on.event(Event=%!screen.element["#window.bot"].on.click%, When="after", Action=goal.call(Name="ShowClaude"))
/ The screen takes the host's input itself — no goal per event, so nothing waits behind a goal
/ (a question waiting for the click that answers it).
- screen.listen(Screen=%screen%)
- stop %browser%

Question
/ The question in a dialog on the desktop, lifted above every window; the answer is what the person
/ chose (a permission: y, a or n; a question: what they typed). The question is %message%.
- window.call(Name="AskShow", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={question: %message%}); variable.set(Name=%above%, Value=%!data%)
- send %above% to %screen%
- window.call(Name="AskAnswer", Window=%browser.desktop%); variable.set(Name=%answer%, Value=%!data%)
- send %answer.below% to %screen%
- return %answer.text%

ShowError
/ An error written to an error channel is %message%, and where it happened %where% ({goal, step}; there only when
/ it happened in a goal): the desktop lists it (what, where, when) and counts it on the taskbar.
- window.call(Name="ErrorShow", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={error: %message%, where: %where%})

Desktop
/ The desktop page asks: {"open": url} opens a window; {"window": "focus|minimize|…", "id"}
/ goes to the screen; {"files"} shows the desktop's files; {"edit": path} opens one in Writer.
/ Writer asks: {"save": path, "text"}, {"list": folder}, {"load": path}, {"create": path},
/ {"build": path}, {"run": goal}; "from" is the window that asked. Claude's box (on the desktop)
/ asks: {"say": what the person wrote, "about": {"window", "title"}}.
- set %asked% to %!data%
- if %asked.open%, call Open
- if %asked.window%, call Command
- if %asked.files%, call Files
- if %asked.edit%, call Edit
- if %asked.save%, call Save
- if %asked.list%, call List
- if %asked.load%, call Load
- if %asked.create%, call Create
- if %asked.build%, call Build
- if %asked.run%, call Run
- condition.if(Left=%asked.say%) { goal.call(Name="Say") }
- if %asked.update%, call Update in parallel

Update
/ New files for this shell from the host (its %!app.parent%; staged on Windows in shell.next): each written into the
/ shell's folder, then the desktop loads again. Pages show the change now; a changed goal (.build/*.pr) is used when
/ PlangOS starts again. No image, nothing in /home/plang touched.
- set %update% to []
- goal.call(Name=%!app.parent.goal["ShellUpdate"]%); variable.set(Name=%update%, Value=%!data%)
/ the system writes the system's files: os/** is written by the system actor only — a user's program writing there is asked
- goal.call(Name="InstallAll", Parameter={files: %update%}, Actor="system")
- condition.if(Left=%update%, Operator="isnotempty") { goal.call(Name="Updated") }

Version
/ The host says what runs ("plang a61a8c2b7, image c88437e5"); the desktop shows it on the taskbar. A host from
/ before Version has none to say: nothing shown, no error.
- goal.call(Name=%!app.parent.goal["Version"]%); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="NoVersion")]); variable.set(Name=%version%, Value=%!data%)
- window.call(Name="VersionShow", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={version: %version%})

NoVersion
- set %version% to ""

InstallAll
- foreach %files%, call Install sent=%item%

Install
/ %sent.path% is where in PlangOS (/system/plangos/desktop.html): the host says it whole
- save %sent.content% to %sent.path%

Updated
- window.reload(Window=%browser.desktop%, Browser=%browser%)
- goal.call(Name="Files")
- window.call(Name="ShowUpdated", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={files: %update%})

Open
- open window %asked.open% in %browser%

Command
- send %asked% to %screen%

Files
/ the desktop's files: what is in the app's Desktop/, shown as icons. A path that starts with "/"
/ is in the app (/home/plang); without it, it would be beside this goal, in the os folder.
- list files in '/Desktop', write to %files%
/ (formal: "call X in %window%" is a page's function, which the builder takes for a goal)
- window.call(Name="ShowFiles", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={files: %files%})

Edit
/ a file opens in Writer, in a window of its own: what it holds — a text file its text, a json file
/ its value
- open window 'file:///opt/plang/os/system/plangos/app/writer/start.html' in %browser%, write to %writer%
- read %asked.edit%, write to %content%
/ (call Show file=%asked.edit%, content=%content% in %writer% — formal until builder issue 41 is fixed)
- window.call(Name="Show", Window=%writer%, Parameter={file: %asked.edit%, content: %content%})

Save
/ Ctrl+S in Writer: the file's format writes what Writer sends — a text file's text, a json file's value
- save %asked.content% to %asked.save%
- window.call(Name="Saved", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%)

List
/ Writer's Open and New: the files in a folder and its folders
- list files in %asked.list% recursive, write to %files%
- window.call(Name="ShowList", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={folder: %asked.list%, files: %files%})

Load
/ Writer's Open: another file in the same window
- read %asked.load%, write to %content%
- window.call(Name="Show", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={file: %asked.load%, content: %content%})

Create
/ Writer's New: an empty file, opened in the same window; the desktop shows it
- file.save(Path=%asked.create%, Value="")
- window.call(Name="Show", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={file: %asked.create%, content: ""})
- call Files

Build
/ Writer's ▶ (build): plang builds the app — its own process, as plang build does anywhere; what it
/ wrote, and how it ended, go back to the window.
- terminal.start(App="plang", Parameter=["build", "--llmservice=openai"]); on.timeout(After="PT10M"); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="BuildFailed")]); variable.set(Name=%built%, Value=%!data%)
- window.call(Name="Built", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={output: %built%, error: %built!error%, code: %built!exitCode%})

BuildFailed
/ plang couldn't be started (or timed out): the window hears it, rather than waiting on
- window.call(Name="Built", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={error: %!error.Message%, code: -1})

Run
/ Writer's ▶ (run): the goal runs in a plang of its own (this one's output is the screen); what it
/ wrote goes back to the window.
- terminal.start(App="plang", Parameter=[%asked.run%]); on.timeout(After="PT5M"); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="RunFailed")]); variable.set(Name=%ran%, Value=%!data%)
- window.call(Name="Ran", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={output: %ran%, error: %ran!error%, code: %ran!exitCode%})

RunFailed
- window.call(Name="Ran", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={error: %!error.Message%, code: -1})

ShowClaude
/ ☰ clicked (#window.bot): Claude's box drops down under it — part of the desktop page, lifted above the
/ windows. %!event!result% is the click: its window, where.
- set %click% to %!event!result%
/ the window's page (Writer's: file:///opt/plang/os/system/plangos/app/writer/start.html): the box takes the app from it
- set %clickedPage% to %browser.window[%click.window%].url%
- window.call(Name="AgentShow", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={window: %click.window%, x: %click.x%, y: %click.y%, page: %clickedPage%})

Say
/ The person wrote to Claude about a window. The first time, with what Claude has to know about PlangOS
/ and this window (agent/instructions.md); then it's a conversation. Claude's paths are in the window's app
/ (%asked.about.app%: its folder, as the box worked it out from its page; none for a website).
- set %claudeApp% to %asked.about.app%
- condition.if(Left=%claudeStarted%, Operator="isnotempty") { goal.call(Name="NextWords") }
- condition.if(Left=%claudeStarted%, Operator="isempty") { goal.call(Name="FirstWords") }
/ the conversation runs on its own: a turn waits minutes for Claude, and the screen's clicks (☰ among them) must not
/ wait behind it
- call Turn content=%content% in parallel

FirstWords
- render 'agent/instructions.md', window=%asked.about.window%, title=%asked.about.title%, app=%asked.about.app%, write to %instructions%
/ how every agent in PLang reports back (plang's own: /system/llm/agent.md)
/ (formal: `as text` is dropped by the builder, and a file in a text is its name, not what it holds)
- file.read(Path="/system/llm/agent.md"); variable.set(Name=%standard%, Value=%!data%, Type="text")
- set %content% to [{"type": "text", "text": "%instructions%\n\n%standard%\n\n---\n\n%asked.say%"}]
- set %claudeStarted% to true

NextWords
- set %content% to [{"type": "text", "text": %asked.say%}]

Turn
/ One turn: Claude, in the host (the app that started this one), gets %content%; its words go to the box;
/ the goals it asks for run here, and what they gave is its next turn — until it asks for none.
- goal.call(Name=%!app.parent.goal["Claude"]%, Parameter={message: %content%}); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="ClaudeFailed")]); variable.set(Name=%reply%, Value=%!data%)
- window.call(Name="AgentSays", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={text: %reply.text%, status: %reply.status%, calls: %reply.calls%})
- condition.if(Left=%reply.calls%, Operator="isnotempty") { goal.call(Name="RunCalls") }
- condition.if(Left=%reply.calls%, Operator="isempty") { goal.call(Name="TurnDone") }

ClaudeFailed
- window.call(Name="AgentSays", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={error: %!error.Message%})
- return {text: "", calls: []}

TurnDone
- window.call(Name="AgentDone", Window=%browser.desktop%)

AgentWriting
/ The host calls this while Claude writes its answer (%partial%: the answer so far, half-written JSON): the box
/ shows the words as they come, until the whole answer is there.
- window.call(Name="AgentWriting", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={partial: %partial%})

RunCalls
/ Each goal Claude asked for runs here — only its own, in agent/ — and what it gave goes into its next
/ turn: a screenshot as a picture, anything else as text.
- set %results% to []
- foreach %reply.calls%, call RunCall call=%item%
- goal.call(Name="Turn", Parameter={content: %results%})

RunCall
/ the box shows the call as it starts (what, and why Claude asked for it), and what it gave when it ends
- window.call(Name="AgentCalling", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={goal: %call.goal%, parameters: %call.parameters%, why: %call.why%})
/ then a path Claude gave (in the window's app) is made the shell's own: /start.html in Writer is
/ /system/plangos/app/writer/start.html; /system/… is plang's system as it is
- condition.if(Left=%claudeApp%, Operator="isnotempty") { goal.call(Name="IntoApp") }
- set %agentGoal% to "/system/plangos/agent/%call.goal%"
- goal.call(Name=%agentGoal%, Parameter=%call.parameters%); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="CallFailed")]); variable.set(Name=%got%, Value=%!data%)
- window.call(Name="AgentCalled", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={goal: %call.goal%, got: %got%})
- condition.if(Left=%call.goal%, Operator="==", Right="Screenshot") { goal.call(Name="GavePicture") }
- condition.if(Left=%call.goal%, Operator="!=", Right="Screenshot") { goal.call(Name="GaveText") }

IntoApp
- condition.if(Left=%call.parameters.path%, Operator="isnotempty") { goal.call(Name="PathIntoApp") }

PathIntoApp
- condition.if(Left=%call.parameters.path%, Operator="notstartswith", Right="/system/") { goal.call(Name="AppPath") }

AppPath
/ (made apart first: a member set from a text naming itself is a resolve cycle)
- set %appPath% to "%claudeApp%%call.parameters.path%"
- set %call.parameters.path% to %appPath%

CallFailed
- return "failed: %!error.Message%"

GavePicture
- add {"type": "text", "text": "%call.goal% gave this picture:"} to %results%
- add {"type": "image", "source": {"type": "base64", "media_type": "image/png", "data": %got%}} to %results%

GaveText
- add {"type": "text", "text": "%call.goal% gave: %got%"} to %results%

Window
/ The screen says what happened to a window: the desktop's taskbar shows it. Enter in a
/ window's address field ({"navigate": what was typed, "id"}) sends that window there; its
/ menu's New window, and links opened as tabs ({"open": url}), open a window.
- set %event% to %!data%
- post %event% to %browser.desktop%
- if %event.navigate%, call Navigate
- if %event.open%, call OpenPage
- if %event.tool%, call Tool
- if %event.paste%, call Paste

Navigate
- navigate window %event.id% to %event.navigate% in %browser%

OpenPage
- open window %event.open% in %browser%

Tool
/ One of the app's tools in its window's title bar was clicked ({"tool": "save", "id"}): its page's
/ goal Tool gets it. The page named its tools itself ({"window": "tools", "tools": [...]}).
- window.call(Name="Tool", Window=%event.id%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={tool: %event.tool%})

Paste
/ A page asked for the clipboard as a value ({"window": "paste"}): a copy that knows where it came
/ from, as json; its page's goal Paste gets it.
- window.call(Name="Paste", Window=%event.id%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={value: %event.paste%})
